s10-8-p5 : Block
s10-8-p5 = prose (cons "are different statements: address identity, definitional equality, and a specified relation between interpreted meanings. When the definitions denote structured types, \(\mathsf{SemEq}\) may be an equivalence of those structures; for programs it may instead be a contextual or observational relation. Its type is determined by the interpretations involved. The store can record each relation with its actual evidence and use the strongest available one for the operation being performed. For example, replacing an algebraic representation by an equivalent one can transport dependent laws and operations, whereas a mere hash match is evidence about the stored representation. A proof of a source/target refinement can relate different definitions without identifying their complete semantics." nil)
